color-management-v1: support Windows HDR descriptions and output metadata

Implement the predefined Windows-scRGB and Windows-BT.2100 image
descriptions required by native Wine/Proton Wayland HDR. Upgrade the global
to protocol version 3, report output primary and target luminances separately,
and notify clients when the output image description changes.

Keep Windows-scRGB client-managed: its fixed stimulus mapping is 80 nits per
1.0 and must bypass the compositor's configurable SDR-white gain. Surface
classification helpers let Aqueous also keep native Windows HDR out of its
SDR Auto HDR expansion path.

